 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S441-012\", \"clauses\": {\"read_and_write\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F11\", \"template\": \"Set the clock to show {time_str}{trailing}\", \"reasoning\": \"The write half of the task is produced by F11, which asks the learner to set the clock. The read half is produced by F12, which asks what time the clock shows. F11 is chosen as the single best family for the task clause.\"}, \"time\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F11\", \"template\": \"Set the clock to show {time_str}{trailing}\", \"reasoning\": \"The object of the task, a time, is the value F11 asks the learner to set. time_str draws from precision-derived times, and its printed values are all whole-hour, half-hour or quarter-hour times.\"}, \"hour\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F08\", \"template\": \"{hour}:00\", \"reasoning\": \"F08 gives whole-hour times with hour in the range 1 to 12 (bounds['hour']), which matches the hour clause on a 12-hour analog dial.\"}, \"half_hour\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F11\", \"template\": \"Set the clock to show {time_str}{trailing}\", \"reasoning\": \"F11's time_str printed list includes half-past times at 10, 11, 12 and other hours, so half-hour times are produced by this family.\"}, \"quarter_hour\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F11\", \"template\": \"Set the clock to show {time_str}{trailing}\", \"reasoning\": \"F11's time_str printed list includes quarter-past and quarter-to times (minute values 15 and 45 on several hours), so quarter-hour times are produced by this family.\"}, \"analog_clock\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F12\", \"template\": \"What time does the clock show?\", \"reasoning\": \"F12 presents the clock as the item the learner reads, with the clock shown through interaction_mode. It is the representation the analog_clock clause requires.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F09\", \"F13\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"{hour}:{minute:02d}\", \"{hours}:{minutes:02d}\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F09 fills minute from a domain that is a number in a range from 0 to 59 with basis 'a minute of the hour', not restricted to the hour, half-hour and quarter-hour values this lc names. Its correct_answer and format_data.mcq_options can therefore show minutes such as 7 or 53, which is content beyond the competency's scope and beyond the one_minute and five_minutes precisions only as declared variants. F13 has the same minute range (0 to 59) and also an hours range from 0 to 23 with basis 'an hour of the day'. Values 0 and 13 to 23 cannot be shown on a 12-hour analog dial, and grade 1 quarter 4 has no a.m./p.m. or 24-hour reading in scope (a.m. and p.m. are in NOT_YET_KNOWN). F13 can therefore produce misleading answers and options. F08, F11, F12, F05 and the other hint families stay within 1 to 12 hours and whole, half or quarter minutes, so they pass. Hints F01 to F04 are chosen by minute and cover only 0, 15, 30 and 45. Hints use 'long hand' and 'short hand' where curriculum_vocab names 'minute hand' and 'hour hand'. This is noted but is not a failing finding.\"}",
